      "content": "but he's saying his heart feels fine and he's not having any chest pain or anything. if he's not in pain, why would it be an emergency? it feels like a huge overreaction to send him to the ER just for a few seconds of dizziness. can't we just monitor him for a few hours and see if he stays stable? what's the actual risk if it really is just dehydration?",
